course: dictionary
lesson: 4203
title: Words from the wild
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. Context helps: the words and sentences around a word give you clues. «On a common (open wild land with gorse and bramble) he finds a caravan.» The brackets tell you a common is open wild land, so you can picture it.
explain: Gorse is a plant you can learn from its description. It is a thick, prickly bush with sharp spines and bright yellow flowers. The word prickly is a clue: if something has sharp spines, it can hurt when you touch it, so you should be careful.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Gorse pods pop and fling their seeds out.» If fling means throw out with force, the sentence still makes sense. If you are not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Gorse is a thick, prickly bush with sharp spines and bright yellow flowers.
fact: Gorse flowers smell a little like coconut.
fact: Gorse grows on heaths, hillsides and cliffs, and on wild open land called a common.
fact: Gorse is also called «furze» or «whin».
fact: Gorse is very prickly and burns easily, so keep away from fires near it and be careful when you walk past it.
exercise: «On a common (open wild land with gorse and bramble) he finds a caravan.» What is a common? | A shop that sells food | *Open wild land with gorse and bramble | A kind of caravan | A wooden bucket
exercise: Gorse is very prickly. What does prickly mean? | Soft and warm | *Covered in sharp points that can hurt when touched | Wet and cold | Very loud
exercise: «On a hot summer day on the heath you can hear gorse pods pop and fling their seeds out.» What does fling mean? | Gently fold | Dry in the sun | Eat slowly | *Throw out with force
test: Gorse is also called another name, which means the same thing. Which one? | Bramble | Heather | *Furze | Ivy
test: «Gorse pods dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst.» When do the pods burst? | At night in the cold | *On hot dry days | When the bush is picked | In winter rain
exam: The saying «When gorse is out of bloom, kissing's out of fashion» suggests what? | Gorse only flowers at night | Gorse only flowers in one month of the year | Gorse never flowers | *Some gorse is in flower nearly all year, so there is nearly always a time for kissing
